[[:db/retract 17592186220842 :answer-field/choices 17592186220848] [:db/retract 17592186220842 :answer-field/choices 17592186220843] [:db/retract 17592186220842 :answer-field/choices 17592186220844] [:db/retract 17592186220842 :answer-field/choices 17592186220845] [:db/retract 17592186220842 :answer-field/choices 17592186220846] [:db/retract 17592186220842 :answer-field/choices 17592186220847] [:db/retract 17592186220905 :answer-field/choices 17592186220906] [:db/retract 17592186220905 :answer-field/choices 17592186220907] [:db/retract 17592186220905 :answer-field/choices 17592186220908] [:db/retract 17592186220905 :answer-field/choices 17592186220909] [:db/retract 17592186316983 :answer-field/choices 17592186316476] {:db/id 17592186222027 :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-8x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{2}+1∼-\\frac{13}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-\\frac{13}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-2,2),$\n\n- continuous on $[-2,2),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-2)=F(2),$ if we extend the value at $x=2$ using the formula $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}+1.$\n\nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4{x}^{2}+1) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{13}{3})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ -8x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ -8x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ -8x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e1109bc7-547a-500f-b40b-e4d37aec3c09" "answer-field-bf744a44-3007-5aee-a43d-ad3854082722" "answer-field-28452a53-092e-519f-8707-b42d65bf6fbf" "answer-field-7efb2097-cd14-54a1-b0fa-f72890b9e249"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220842 :answer-field/correct "answer-73b3831c-2550-547a-9666-08932392aa02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36ace1c9-2f52-5838-8105-d6761b6f44e5" "answer-73b3831c-2550-547a-9666-08932392aa02" "answer-fda62ace-a6e8-57a0-8947-9301332fd088" "answer-b6477d72-545a-55fc-9970-dbb46ef4dc84" "answer-cd3c6f01-d506-5569-bd88-65579a986ff7" "answer-08d5e60e-7f26-5a6e-af43-a4123987b83e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36ace1c9-2f52-5838-8105-d6761b6f44e5" :answer/id #uuid "36ace1c9-2f52-5838-8105-d6761b6f44e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73b3831c-2550-547a-9666-08932392aa02" :answer/id #uuid "73b3831