ay integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316983 :answer-field/correct 17592186315537 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-34e3151a-47c8-57be-a129-fae3a26f1727" :activity/id #uuid "34e3151a-47c8-57be-a129-fae3a26f1727" :activity/title "Differentiating and Integrating Fourier Series" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050010 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-6c9ca774-b4f6-520b-b234-3903b9ac3e3c" "step-90354e30-ad99-522d-adc0-19a8645a92ab" "step-39822680-80da-5f81-9803-335e6ef154f4"] :activity/first-step "step-6c9ca774-b4f6-520b-b234-3903b9ac3e3c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6c9ca774-b4f6-520b-b234-3903b9ac3e3c" :step/id #uuid "6c9ca774-b4f6-520b-b234-3903b9ac3e3c" :step/content 17592186222027 :step/next "step-90354e30-ad99-522d-adc0-19a8645a92ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-90354e30-ad99-522d-adc0-19a8645a92ab" :step/id #uuid "90354e30-ad99-522d-adc0-19a8645a92ab" :step/content 17592186222036 :step/next "step-39822680-80da-5f81-9803-335e6ef154f4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-39822680-80da-5f81-9803-335e6ef154f4" :step/id #uuid "39822680-80da-5f81-9803-335e6ef154f4" :step/content 17592186317389 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198381 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19215bce-b998-5155-b240-d07f98b470fa" "question-dfe9429c-8eb3-53cb-93d2-56d808d34d21" "question-fec8c045-97d0-52ff-98f7-547a00ead0cc" "question-78fbce00-db2e-5209-8254-7392130a0e24"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198023 :question/problem "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $1 \\div (-7).$" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $({\\color{blue}{1}})$ by a negative one $({\\color{red}{-7}}).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n![](images/b3/b3fdb7fe402f5e8ebfdf8502e8173faaaa11082ed9f618884cd1770e764ffaac.svg)\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n1 \\div 7 = \\dfrac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-7)}} = {\\color{red}-\\dfrac{1}{7}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198382 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ab03c0c5-9201-5f34-bca6-0752e2243d74" "question-c0034021-3171-56a7-bc93-8c5725afb68c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198024 :question/problem "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $(-5) \\div (-3).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we are dividing a negative number $({\\color{red}-5})$ by another negative number $({\\color{red}-3}).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n![](images/cc/cce63c47aea469b99cccad529462e33e193ff094efb7d3535cf8ca095d8c23a9.svg)\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5 \\div 3 = 1 \\,\\textrm{R}\\, 2 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue} 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198383 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ec1af280-a6fd-52ab-9d3d-511d96573c0d" "question-93f4a5cf-cbff-5d1e-aa34-eea593763369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198025 :question/problem "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{\\bbox[1pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A positive number can be obtained if we divide two numbers that are either both positive or both negative.\n\nSo, given a positive fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{-14}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the numerator on the right-hand side is negative $({{\\color{red}-3}}).$ Therefore, the missing denominator must be $({{\\color{red}-14}}){:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{\\bbox[2pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\color{red}-14}}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-19215bce-b998-5155-b240-d07f98b470fa" :question/id #uuid "19215bce-b998-5155-b240-d07f98b470fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-161945" :question/problem "$8÷(-3)$ is equivalent to" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $(8)$ by a negative one $(-3).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n8÷(-3)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n8÷3=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n8÷(-3)=-\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-33d2f3ec-f340-5841-8ec0-b682b902fa25"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-33d2f3ec-f340-5841-8ec0-b682b902fa25" :answer-field/id #uuid "33d2f3ec-f340-5841-8ec0-b682b902fa25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea8e52db-67e4-55ce-bc43-03be25f38464" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3123abe7-0892-58f4-8d1e-3a72a88a0b11" "answer-39b17254-625f-5a30-ae52-43437b1b9a8b" "answer-ea8e52db-67e4-55ce-bc43-03be25f38464" "answer-4677b5c0-c189-5884-92fd-ccb093aede16" "answer-19da7377-89ec-5b18-8178-f6b5883475d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3123abe7-0892-58f4-8d1e-3a72a88a0b11" :answer/id #uuid "3123abe7-0892-58f4-8d1e-3a72a88a0b11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39b17254-625f-5a30-ae52-43437b1b9a8b" :answer/id #uuid "39b17254-625f-5a30-ae52-43437b1b9a8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea8e52db-67e4-55ce-bc43-03be25f38464" :answer/id #uuid "ea8e52db-67e4-55ce-bc43-03be25f38464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4677b5c0-c189-5884-92fd-ccb093aede16" :answer/id #uuid "4677b5c0-c189-5884-92fd-ccb093aede16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19da7377-89ec-5b18-8178-f6b5883475d2" :answer/id #uuid "19da7377-89ec-5b18-8178-f6b5883475d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dfe9429c-8eb3-53cb-93d2-56d808d34d21" :question/id #uuid "dfe9429c-8eb3-53cb-93d2-56d808d34d21" :question/math-academy-id "q-161937" :question/problem "$(-4)÷9$ is equivalent to" :question/worked-solution "Here, we are dividing a negative number $(-4)$ by a positive one $(9).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-4)÷9=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n4÷9=\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-4)÷9=-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e835be37-7ff2-545e-ba4c-6a2dc207cad7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e835be37-7ff2-545e-ba4c-6a2dc207cad7" :answer-field/id #uuid "e835be37-7ff2-545e-ba4c-6a2dc207cad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8938986-581f-53cd-a487-69122980af2e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5567f553-33e7-5be0-bffd-95d5c4882598" "answer-f8938986-581f-53cd-a487-69122980af2e" "answer-3d849503-b540-5797-b860-d39575989e91" "answer-90d9dbc4-d216-58a8-aaf0-4ba18daa0493" "answer-b0c23a64-8974-5c0f-8638-380eff14b23a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5567f553-33e7-5be0-bffd-95d5c4882598" :answer/id #uuid "5567f553-33e7-5be0-bffd-95d5c4882598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8938986-581f-53cd-a487-69122980af2e" :answer/id #uuid "f8938986-581f-53cd-a487-69122980af2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d849503-b540-5797-b860-d39575989e91" :answer/id #uuid "3d849503-b540-5797-b860-d39575989e91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answ